Where computing, innovation and collaboration come together. 🤝

The Crescent team led by Mr.Abdul Qadir, Pro Chancellor, BSACIST, and Chairman, CIIC and AIC-CIIC, had the opportunity to visit the Georgia Institute of Technology’s College of Computing https://t.co/AP6QQqbsPi and meet Dr.Vivek Sarkar, John P.Imlay Jr., Dean of Computing.

The interaction offered an opportunity to exchange perspectives on the evolving landscape of computing, emerging technologies, research and innovation, while exploring the possibilities for stronger connections between academia and the innovation ecosystem.

As computing continues to shape new approaches to solving complex challenges, conversations that bring together academic expertise, technological capabilities and entrepreneurial ecosystems can open pathways for meaningful knowledge exchange and future collaboration.

The visit added another valuable dimension to Crescent University's engagements with global academic and innovation ecosystems, as we continue to build connections that extend beyond geographical boundaries.

From ideas to impact, meaningful connections are at the heart of every innovation ecosystem.

